{
  "story_id": "S122",
  "title": "Kmt2a loss reveals a context-specific mature-neuronal Nr2f1/Pcdh/Lhx9/Grik2 thalamic regulon",
  "status": "grounded",
  "rejection_reason": null,
  "exact_observed_result": "Kmt2a was FDR-depleted in 151 TH and produced 24 FDR<0.05 genes, including Nr2f1, Pcdh7, and Lhx9 down and Igfbp5/Cx3cl1 up. In 155 MB Glut, Kmt2a and Fnbp1l were the only two FDR rows. Ptprk, Aff4, and Nap1l2 were singleton hits in three other glutamatergic classes, and Las1l did not phenocopy Kmt2a.",
  "biological_interpretation": "Acute KMT2A depletion in the assayed mature neurons resolves to a thalamic neuronal regulon, plus a tiny MB marker, rather than a broad HOX, Dlx2, Meis2, Arc, or LAS1L/5FMC-like collapse.",
